WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.828
Thud, thud, thud.

2
00:00:05.829 --> 00:00:08.831
Katie wrapped her pillow around her ears.

3
00:00:08.832 --> 00:00:12.114
"What’s that noise?" she asked.

4
00:00:12.115 --> 00:00:18.029
Joy rolled over in bed and looked up at the ceiling. Thud, thud.

5
00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:23.536
"Walnuts," Joy answered. "Walnuts are falling on the roof again."

6
00:00:23.537 --> 00:00:29.380
"But I’m trying to sleep!" groaned Katie.

7
00:00:29.381 --> 00:00:32.333
"Sunday morning," mumbled Joy.

8
00:00:32.334 --> 00:00:34.399
Her eyes closed.

9
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.321
Then they opened wide.

10
00:00:36.322 --> 00:00:40.601
"The fiddle!" she cried and threw back her covers.

11
00:00:40.602 --> 00:00:44.455
"Grandpa and I are going to find the fiddle this morning!"

12
00:00:44.456 --> 00:00:48.040
Katie pulled her blanket over her head.

13
00:00:48.041 --> 00:00:51.424
Grandpa and Joy looked for the fiddle in the attic.

14
00:00:51.425 --> 00:00:54.464
They looked in the spare-room closet.

15
00:00:54.465 --> 00:00:58.532
"Have you checked the cedar chests?" asked Mom.

16
00:00:58.533 --> 00:01:03.962
They looked in the chests in Mom and Dad’s room—still no luck.

17
00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:08.746
Then Joy raised the lid on the chest at the end of the hall.

18
00:01:08.747 --> 00:01:14.669
Grandpa moved an old photo album and pulled out two faded quilts.

19
00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:17.941
"There it is!" cried Joy.

20
00:01:17.942 --> 00:01:23.941
Grandpa raised the black case from the chest and opened the lid.

21
00:01:23.942 --> 00:01:31.006
"Oh!" said Joy. She touched the worn wood and broken strings of the violin.

22
00:01:31.007 --> 00:01:34.031
"Poor old thing," she said.

23
00:01:34.032 --> 00:01:38.236
"This fiddle has played a lot of music," said Grandpa.

24
00:01:38.237 --> 00:01:40.865
He picked up a small wooden piece.

25
00:01:40.866 --> 00:01:43.287
"The bridge is bent," he said.

26
00:01:43.288 --> 00:01:45.712
He took out the bow.

27
00:01:45.713 --> 00:01:52.301
"Something’s missing," said Joy, pointing to the ragged hairs on each end of the bow.

28
00:01:52.302 --> 00:01:54.695
She looked hopefully at her grandpa.

29
00:01:54.696 --> 00:01:57.886
"What do you think?" she asked.

30
00:01:57.887 --> 00:02:02.859
"I think that this old fiddle is happy to see the light of day," he said.

31
00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:05.472
"It just needs a few repairs.

32
00:02:05.473 --> 00:02:09.989
While you are at school tomorrow, I’ll take it to the music shop in Bates City.

33
00:02:09.990 --> 00:02:14.346
I’ll find out about getting it fixed and ready to play again!"

34
00:02:14.347 --> 00:02:17.423
"Oh, thank you!" said Joy.

35
00:02:17.424 --> 00:02:24.069
She threw her arms around Grandpa and gave him a big kiss.

36
00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:28.667
The next day, Joy could barely sit still in class.

37
00:02:28.668 --> 00:02:35.347
When the last bell finally rang, Joy hurried to her bicycle.

38
00:02:35.348 --> 00:02:38.049
"Wait for me," called Katie.

39
00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:41.617
But Joy was already flying down the road.

40
00:02:41.618 --> 00:02:46.418
By the time Katie got home, Joy had already disappeared.

41
00:02:46.419 --> 00:02:51.014
Mom sat alone at the kitchen table, looking at the mail.

42
00:02:51.015 --> 00:02:54.690
The violin case lay open on the table.

43
00:02:54.691 --> 00:02:56.992
"Hi, Mom," said Katie.

44
00:02:56.993 --> 00:02:59.906
She dropped her backpack on the floor.

45
00:02:59.907 --> 00:03:04.237
"Hi, honey," said Mom. "You’ve got mail."

46
00:03:04.238 --> 00:03:08.580
Katie’s eyes lit up. "Mail? For me?"

47
00:03:08.581 --> 00:03:11.998
"For you and Joy," said Mom.

48
00:03:11.999 --> 00:03:14.055
Katie ripped open the envelope.

49
00:03:14.056 --> 00:03:17.052
"Hey! What’s this?"

50
00:03:17.053 --> 00:03:20.570
She held a card with autumn leaves on the front.

51
00:03:20.571 --> 00:03:23.312
"You’re invited," she read.

52
00:03:23.313 --> 00:03:25.456
She opened the card.

53
00:03:25.457 --> 00:03:28.240
"A hayride," she said.

54
00:03:28.241 --> 00:03:33.178
"AJ is having a birthday hayride, and we’re invited."

55
00:03:33.179 --> 00:03:35.936
Katie checked the calendar on the kitchen wall.

56
00:03:35.937 --> 00:03:39.609
"It’s two weeks away. I’ll tell Joy."

57
00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:43.951
"She’s out in the garden talking to—," Mom began.

58
00:03:43.952 --> 00:03:48.726
Just then Joy and Grandpa came through the back door.

59
00:03:48.727 --> 00:03:50.923
"Guess what," said Katie.

60
00:03:50.924 --> 00:03:55.659
But she stopped when she saw Joy’s face. "What’s wrong?"

61
00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:59.674
"Joy has some bad news," Mom said to Katie.

62
00:03:59.675 --> 00:04:04.704
"The fiddle needs more repair than we thought," said Grandpa.

63
00:04:04.705 --> 00:04:09.308
"It will cost one hundred dollars," said Joy.

64
00:04:09.309 --> 00:04:13.661
"Yikes!" said Katie. "Now what?"

65
00:04:13.662 --> 00:04:18.378
"We can’t afford to get the fiddle fixed right now," said Joy.

66
00:04:18.379 --> 00:04:20.019
She looked at her mom.

67
00:04:20.020 --> 00:04:23.885
"I’ll just have to wait awhile."

68
00:04:23.886 --> 00:04:27.917
With a big sigh, Joy closed the violin case.

69
00:04:27.918 --> 00:04:31.698
She picked it up and carried it up the stairs.

70
00:04:31.699 --> 00:04:33.604
Nobody said a word.

71
00:04:33.605 --> 00:04:36.921
Then Katie remembered the hayride.

72
00:04:36.922 --> 00:04:41.787
"Wait, Joy!" she yelled. "There’s good news too!"

73
00:04:41.788 --> 00:04:46.899
She ran upstairs after her sister.

